    {
      "id": "87fb3abe-9833-4a12-8436-f2d6c863b39b",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1000,
        "content": "## Draft context-aware Gmail replies with Claude, approve by label to auto-send\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow drafts replies to incoming Gmail with the full conversation history in mind and never sends anything on its own. New unread emails are normalized, the entire thread is fetched and condensed, and Claude classifies the email, skips noise, and drafts a reply that mirrors your real writing examples under strict per-category rules. Drafts wait in the Gmail thread while a state row is saved to the Pending Replies sheet, 1 row per thread, so if another email arrives before you approve, the newest draft replaces the stale one. Complaints and urgent emails alert you immediately. A second flow polls for threads you label send-approved, sends the matching pending reply in the thread, marks the row sent, deletes the leftover draft, and removes the approval label so future replies in that thread wait for a fresh approval.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Gmail credentials in the Gmail nodes and Anthropic credentials in the Claude model node.\n- Create a Google Sheet with 2 tabs. Email Log with header row: timestamp, from, subject, category, urgency, draft_created, escalate, reason. Pending Replies with header row: thread_id, message_id, draft_id, to, subject, body, status, created_at. Select it in the 4 Google Sheets nodes.\n- Create a Gmail label named send-approved.\n- Edit Set Business Profile: business name, tone, key facts, signature, alert email, and paste 2 or 3 real replies you have written.\n- Test with an email to yourself: leave it unread, run the flow, review the draft, apply the label, run the approval flow.\n\n### Customization\n\nTune the tone, facts and writing examples in Set Business Profile, swap the escalation alert for Slack, tighten the trigger query to specific senders, or change the approval polling frequency."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "81804375-5782-4096-bd41-378616b116a8",
